## Track 1: Five Threads Meet After Beat One

**Story & Context:** At 124 BPM, Austėja opens with a five-attack kanklės Lattice Cell split between low and high string zones. Serge programs a compact kick-and-clap groove but deliberately leaves beat one relatively plain. The first bright woodblock and clap combination lands later, at the point where the fifth attack of one cell coincides with the third attack of another, creating the track’s False Downbeat. Rasa answers with one dry suspended-second Wurlitzer shell after the coincidence rather than before it. Yao replaces every fourth low tom with a dundun bass stroke. Mireille enters with a short flugelhorn fifth only when the electric bass drops out. Midway through, Thread Swap moves the lowest kanklės note into the upper register while preserving the same rhythmic cell, making the groove feel lighter without changing tempo or harmony.

